  {%- comment -%}
    Outline heart for the header icon row. `heart` above is a solid white glyph on a
    non-square 15x13 viewBox, drawn for the product card's translucent pill over a photo;
    dropped into the header it renders a different shape family, ignores `color` entirely
    (its fill is hardcoded white, so it barely reads on the pale icon button) and sits at a
    different optical height because the viewBox is not square.

    This one follows the exact recipe the header's own icons use -- see 'account' and
    'search': a square 0 0 16 16 viewBox, `fill="none"`, `stroke="currentColor"` and
    `stroke-width="1.3"`. That makes the rendered stroke 1.3px, identical to the account
    icon, and within 0.07px of the cart (whose 25x26 viewBox scales its stroke-width 2
    down to 1.23px). Inheriting currentColor is also what gives it the same colour and
    hover behaviour as its neighbours for free.
  {%- endcomment -%}
